WEBVTT

00:02.045 --> 00:04.047
[Man] Previously on lost:

00:04.130 --> 00:05.882
[Jack] Who are you?
— Daniel Faraday.

00:05.965 --> 00:07.342
I'm here to rescue you.

00:09.469 --> 00:12.222
I just almost died
jumping out of a helicopter

00:12.305 --> 00:14.891
because you called us for help.
— she's lying.

00:14.974 --> 00:17.060
Whatever they came for, it isn't us.

00:17.143 --> 00:19.229
Hey. Is that from your chopper?

00:19.312 --> 00:22.857
Yeah. That, uh...
Yeah, they reduce the weight load.

00:22.941 --> 00:25.109
What's this for? — uh...

00:25.193 --> 00:27.070
Rescuing you and your people...

00:27.153 --> 00:30.365
I can't really say
it's our primary objective.

00:36.996 --> 00:39.374
[Clock ticking]

00:54.555 --> 00:56.849
Hello. I'm sorry I'm late.

00:56.933 --> 00:59.227
You must be Dr. Burke. — Juliet.

00:59.310 --> 01:02.188
Juliet. I'm Harper stanhope.

01:02.272 --> 01:04.357
Please sit.

01:06.442 --> 01:08.236
Today is just a meet and greet

01:08.319 --> 01:10.488
so that we can get to know each other.

01:10.571 --> 01:14.575
Please don't take this the wrong way,
but I really don't think I need therapy.

01:16.160 --> 01:19.122
How about we call it "talking"
instead of therapy?

01:23.042 --> 01:25.169
Let's talk.

01:25.920 --> 01:28.214
So you've been here a week...

01:29.048 --> 01:32.010
And what's
your least favorite part so far?

01:32.844 --> 01:35.430
I don't like being treated
like a celebrity.

01:35.513 --> 01:37.515
And is that surprising?

01:37.598 --> 01:41.227
You're big news right now.
— yes, I know.

01:42.854 --> 01:45.648
I guess I don't like being
the center of attention.

01:46.816 --> 01:48.693
It makes me feel isolated.

01:50.570 --> 01:51.904
Alone.

01:54.866 --> 01:58.578
Well, maybe you feel
that all eyes are on you...

01:59.454 --> 02:01.664
But you're not a celebrity.

02:01.748 --> 02:05.877
And soon enough you'll realize that
you're no different than anyone here.

02:05.960 --> 02:09.630
I know. I never meant that I...
— yes?

02:09.714 --> 02:11.966
Harper, I'm sorry for the interruption.

02:12.050 --> 02:16.012
I know you don't like me busting in,
but Ben would like to see the doc.

02:18.931 --> 02:20.808
She's all yours, Tom.

02:23.603 --> 02:26.189
It was nice talking to you, Juliet.

02:26.272 --> 02:28.316
Welcome to the island.

02:31.569 --> 02:33.363
Harper's a real piece of work.

02:33.446 --> 02:37.116
But if you give her a week, she'll
have you crying about your daddy.

02:37.200 --> 02:39.911
I'm speaking
from personal experience here.

02:44.457 --> 02:46.626
Welcome to your humble abode.

02:48.419 --> 02:49.796
This is for me?

02:50.588 --> 02:52.090
The whole house?

02:52.173 --> 02:55.885
You're here to help us with some
very important research, Juliet.

02:55.968 --> 02:58.054
We pulled out all the stops.

02:59.931 --> 03:02.266
Two bedrooms, two baths,
washer, dryer.

03:03.142 --> 03:06.020
Fresh linens, a well—stocked fridge.
— [laughing]

03:06.104 --> 03:09.774
And I know you love the opera.
We have all the classics on cd.

03:11.192 --> 03:12.860
Ben, this is amazing.

03:12.944 --> 03:15.988
Seriously, you shouldn't have gone
to all the trouble.

03:16.072 --> 03:18.199
I'm only gonna be here for six months.

03:18.282 --> 03:19.826
Right, of course, but...

03:21.911 --> 03:23.913
We want you to feel at home.

03:32.004 --> 03:34.048
Need some help?

03:34.132 --> 03:37.427
I'm fine. I just can't seem
to get it steady.

03:37.510 --> 03:39.178
[Both grunting]

03:44.642 --> 03:48.729
Why are you going to all this trouble
when we're about to leave this island?

03:48.813 --> 03:51.065
We still need somewhere
to sleep tonight.

03:51.149 --> 03:54.360
Juliet, have you seen
Charlotte and Faraday?

03:54.444 --> 03:56.696
All their stuff's gone.
— no, I haven't.

03:56.779 --> 04:01.033
You have the sat—phone, right?
— [speaking Korean]

04:01.117 --> 04:03.453
He saw them going into the jungle.

04:06.164 --> 04:08.124
Why didn't he say anything?

04:08.207 --> 04:09.667
[Speaking Korean]

04:11.878 --> 04:14.589
You said they are friends.

04:18.926 --> 04:20.261
Aren't they?

04:22.388 --> 04:25.850
We got a lot of ground to cover,
so let's fan out.

04:25.933 --> 04:29.687
If you cut their trail,
call out to me, I'll come to you.

04:39.864 --> 04:42.325
[Thunder rumbling]

04:54.253 --> 04:57.590
[Indistinct whispering]

05:00.760 --> 05:02.512
[Whispering continues]

05:10.937 --> 05:13.022
Hello, Juliet.

05:13.105 --> 05:14.941
Long time, no see.

05:38.464 --> 05:39.882
What are you doing here?

05:39.966 --> 05:43.844
I came to deliver a message...
From Ben.

05:44.637 --> 05:48.099
The two people you're looking for,
Faraday and Lewis,

05:48.182 --> 05:50.059
they're headed to the tempest.

05:50.643 --> 05:53.312
And if they figure out
how to deploy that gas...

05:54.272 --> 05:58.526
Then everyone on this island
is going to die.

06:00.987 --> 06:04.156
Why don't you stop them?
— because Ben wants you to go.

06:04.240 --> 06:07.702
How can Ben know where they are
when he's a prisoner?

06:07.785 --> 06:10.496
Ben is exactly where he wants to be.

06:18.254 --> 06:21.465
How am I supposed to stop them?
— by pointing the gun

06:21.549 --> 06:24.093
and pulling the trigger.

06:24.176 --> 06:25.303
[Jack] Hey!

06:27.930 --> 06:30.057
Who are you?

06:31.350 --> 06:33.352
I'm an old friend of Juliet's.

06:35.062 --> 06:38.608
I just told her where the people
you're looking for are headed.

06:38.691 --> 06:41.152
Maybe you and your gun can go too.

06:42.987 --> 06:45.573
[Indistinct whispering]

07:05.760 --> 07:08.346
[Sobbing]

07:15.728 --> 07:17.229
[Clattering]

07:25.571 --> 07:27.281
You ok?

07:28.949 --> 07:32.870
I was just looking for some gauze.
I didn't know anyone was here.

07:39.126 --> 07:41.045
How'd you manage that?

07:41.128 --> 07:44.674
I, um...
I work over at the power station.

07:44.757 --> 07:47.009
I pressed up against a transformer.

07:48.719 --> 07:51.138
Take a seat.
Let me take a look at it.

07:59.730 --> 08:01.607
You're Burke, right?

08:02.316 --> 08:03.651
The baby doctor.

08:05.986 --> 08:08.030
What gave me away?

08:10.700 --> 08:12.993
I heard we lost henrietta this morning.

08:15.371 --> 08:17.206
It's ok. It's not your fault.

08:17.289 --> 08:19.709
Pregnant women
are dying on this island.

08:21.585 --> 08:23.963
I was brought here to help fix that.

08:25.464 --> 08:27.341
80 whose fault is it?

08:28.217 --> 08:31.971
Believe me, no one expects you
to fix it overnight.

08:36.642 --> 08:39.478
You have anyone to talk to?
Any friends here?

08:42.648 --> 08:45.735
Maybe Harper. — Harper hates me.

08:45.818 --> 08:48.028
We only talk because we have to.

08:48.112 --> 08:52.491
I get the feeling that she's a mean
and spiteful person.

08:55.494 --> 08:57.496
She's my wife.

08:59.290 --> 09:00.708
She's your wife? — mm—hmm.

09:03.335 --> 09:06.756
I'm sorry.
— no, don't worry about it. It's ok.

09:06.839 --> 09:09.175
Ok, you're... you're set.

09:11.802 --> 09:13.512
Much obliged, ma'am.

09:16.682 --> 09:20.352
Hey, I know this place can wear on you,

09:20.436 --> 09:22.271
but if you need to talk...

09:23.522 --> 09:25.191
I'm around.

09:25.274 --> 09:26.484
Good to know.

09:27.443 --> 09:33.115
Oh, um, if you promise not to tell
your wife what I said about her...

09:33.991 --> 09:37.703
I won't tell anyone you lied
about how you hurt your arm.

09:40.122 --> 09:42.792
I know a chemical burn when I see one.

09:48.047 --> 09:49.924
You got a deal.

09:54.220 --> 09:56.222
Uh, by the way...

09:58.182 --> 09:59.809
I'm goodwin.

10:00.476 --> 10:02.144
Juliet.

10:12.655 --> 10:15.491
Faraday and Charlotte
are heading for the tempest.

10:15.574 --> 10:18.828
The tempest?
— It's safer if I don't talk about it.

10:18.911 --> 10:20.496
No, talk about it, please.

10:20.579 --> 10:23.457
It's an electrical station
that powers the island.

10:23.541 --> 10:25.417
Why would they go there?

10:25.501 --> 10:27.211
Hey.

10:28.712 --> 10:31.340
If there's something
you need to tell me...

10:31.423 --> 10:33.175
Now's the time to do it.

10:35.761 --> 10:37.847
What I need is for you to help me.

10:37.930 --> 10:39.682
Will you help me?

10:46.772 --> 10:50.401
If we move all night,
maybe we can still catch them.

10:54.446 --> 10:55.447
Thank you.

11:05.624 --> 11:07.626
I think it's that way.

11:11.839 --> 11:14.592
What happens if I...

11:16.802 --> 11:18.637
What if I can't do it?

11:22.433 --> 11:23.893
Look at me.

11:25.936 --> 11:28.522
I know you can do this.

11:31.567 --> 11:33.235
We should get going.

11:38.616 --> 11:39.867
Come on.

11:42.953 --> 11:46.415
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
It's ok. It's ok. It's Kate.

11:56.884 --> 11:58.260
So they have miles?

11:59.970 --> 12:03.265
Yeah, but he's fine.
They're treating him fine.

12:03.974 --> 12:06.477
I thought you two
were with Jack at the beach.

12:08.228 --> 12:10.189
What are you guys doing out here?

12:11.523 --> 12:14.777
Jack was trying to communicate
with Sayid and Desmond,

12:14.860 --> 12:17.738
but the sat—phone ran out ofjuice.

12:17.821 --> 12:21.325
It's totally dead.
There's no way we can call the boat.

12:22.117 --> 12:26.705
So we volunteered to get spare batteries
out the packs we threw out the chopper.

12:28.499 --> 12:32.461
So if you threw your pack
from the chopper,

12:32.544 --> 12:33.587
what's that?

12:35.547 --> 12:39.176
This, uh... I just borrowed this.

12:46.558 --> 12:48.227
Go ahead, Dan, show her.

12:56.777 --> 12:57.903
Baflenes, huh?

12:57.987 --> 12:59.738
What's this...? [Grunts]

13:12.668 --> 13:15.254
That woman, what was her name?
— Harper.

13:16.088 --> 13:19.341
The two of you friends?
— not exactly.

13:19.425 --> 13:22.845
She was my therapist.
— you people had therapists?

13:22.928 --> 13:26.265
It's very stressful
being an other, Jack.

13:28.642 --> 13:32.646
Seemed hostile, even for a therapist.
— there are things from your past

13:32.730 --> 13:36.900
you'd rather not talk about.
— yeah. You read them all in my file.

13:38.402 --> 13:41.030
Trust me, Jack,
you don't want to see my file.

13:45.743 --> 13:48.996
The problem occurs somewhere
during the second trimester

13:49.079 --> 13:51.707
when the mother's immune system
is triggered.

13:51.790 --> 13:54.084
The white blood cell count plummets.

13:54.168 --> 13:58.130
It's like the immune system
turns on the fetus.

13:59.631 --> 14:01.467
May I? — sure.

14:08.057 --> 14:11.727
Any thought yet on a cause?
— It's really too early to tell,

14:11.810 --> 14:16.231
but only women who have conceived
on the island does it happen to which...

14:16.315 --> 14:18.108
Hey, Juliet.

14:21.320 --> 14:23.155
Ben, I didn't know you were here.

14:24.740 --> 14:27.910
Ethan's out sick.
I have an extra egg salad on rye.

14:27.993 --> 14:30.329
I was just checking if Juliet wants it.

14:30.412 --> 14:32.206
Thanks. I already ate.

14:32.289 --> 14:35.042
I have an appointment
with your wife in ten minutes.

14:35.125 --> 14:38.003
Great. Tell her I said hi.

14:39.171 --> 14:40.839
Oh, will do.

14:42.091 --> 14:44.551
Ben? — no, I'm fine.

14:59.608 --> 15:03.195
So, Juliet, what do you think of Ben?

15:05.322 --> 15:07.366
He's great.

15:08.242 --> 15:11.120
Very smart and intense.

15:11.203 --> 15:13.247
Challenging.

15:13.997 --> 15:16.792
He's been really good to me.
— of course he has.

15:16.875 --> 15:18.919
You look just like her.

15:20.003 --> 15:21.213
I'm sorry?

15:21.296 --> 15:23.924
I see you and my husband
have become friendly.

15:27.928 --> 15:30.764
Yeah. He's great.

15:31.723 --> 15:33.809
He's been really helpful.

15:37.062 --> 15:39.690
When did you start sleeping with him?

15:44.486 --> 15:48.157
Look, Juliet, I'm not an idiot,
sojust tell me.

15:48.240 --> 15:50.200
When did it start?

15:52.077 --> 15:55.414
Ok, I'm not doing this. We're done.

15:55.497 --> 15:58.458
No, please respect me enough
to spare me the pretense

15:58.542 --> 16:00.627
that you are actually offended.

16:00.711 --> 16:04.089
I know. I followed you.

16:07.050 --> 16:09.261
Watched you.

16:16.852 --> 16:19.354
I'm sorry.
— It doesn't matter anymore.

16:19.438 --> 16:21.315
But what does matter

16:21.398 --> 16:24.610
is that you listen to me
and that you believe me.

16:27.613 --> 16:32.743
Now if you continue to have
a relationship with goodwin...

16:33.869 --> 16:35.871
There will be consequences.

16:37.789 --> 16:41.877
I don't want him to get hurt.
— I would never hurt him.

16:41.960 --> 16:44.046
I am not talking about you.

16:44.129 --> 16:46.924
I am talking about Ben.

16:54.306 --> 16:56.558
Hi, John.

16:56.642 --> 16:58.352
Hey, Claire.

17:02.105 --> 17:04.066
Is there something I can do for you?

17:04.149 --> 17:06.401
I want to know
what's going on with miles.

17:06.526 --> 17:08.237
Right now not a whole lot.

17:08.320 --> 17:12.658
I'm bringing him food and water
until he decides to talk.

17:14.159 --> 17:16.662
I'd like to talk to him myself.

17:17.621 --> 17:19.414
Why would you want to do that?

17:19.498 --> 17:22.084
John, we have to find out
who these people are

17:22.167 --> 17:26.255
and where they came from... and why
they're not interested in rescuing us.

17:26.338 --> 17:29.216
You don't think I'll get that?
— no, I...

17:30.968 --> 17:33.929
I just think we might be
taking the wrong approach.

17:34.012 --> 17:37.266
I mean, you killed one,
Ben shot one.

17:37.349 --> 17:39.601
Now we're holding one prisoner.

17:39.685 --> 17:43.772
You know, it's not hard to understand
why they might think we're hostile.

17:46.149 --> 17:48.568
I might be just
a little less intimidating.

17:50.570 --> 17:52.990
It's not going to happen, Claire.
— John.

17:53.073 --> 17:55.951
You do remember what Charlie said
about these people.

17:56.034 --> 17:58.870
All Charlie said
was whose boat it isn't.

18:00.330 --> 18:03.709
Don't you want to know whose boat it is?

18:12.592 --> 18:13.760
[Keys clattering]

18:24.563 --> 18:28.066
Rabbit today?
— we're running out of chickens.

18:31.361 --> 18:34.323
This didn't have a number on it, did it?

18:36.533 --> 18:39.411
Eat, change. Put your laundry
and dishes by the door.

18:39.494 --> 18:41.872
I'll be back to collect them
in 15 minutes.

18:41.955 --> 18:44.541
So has the revolution begun yet?

18:50.464 --> 18:52.174
What are you talking about?

18:53.633 --> 18:56.887
Well, you're the leader now.
I know it's a tough position.

18:57.554 --> 19:01.183
You have to deal with all those people
second—guessing decisions.

19:01.266 --> 19:04.061
It starts out so innocently, doesn't it?

19:04.144 --> 19:08.315
A question here, a comment there.
And then if you're not careful,

19:08.398 --> 19:11.777
you find you have a full—blown
insurrection on your hands.

19:11.860 --> 19:15.906
Believe me, your people
are gonna be so angry

19:15.989 --> 19:19.284
when they realize
you still don't have a plan.

19:21.745 --> 19:24.498
And I assume you have a plan.

19:24.581 --> 19:26.458
I always have a plan.

19:26.541 --> 19:29.878
Does it involve
you raising $3.2 million?

19:33.173 --> 19:34.966
That's a lot of money.

19:35.967 --> 19:37.427
Wait.

19:38.804 --> 19:40.931
Maybe this will get you started.

19:43.475 --> 19:45.727
Put your laundry and dishes
by the door.

19:47.562 --> 19:50.816
I can help you, John.
We have shared interests.

19:51.942 --> 19:55.362
Or at least a common enemy.
— our friends on the freighter.

19:55.445 --> 19:59.157
Not them. The one they work for.

20:01.660 --> 20:03.829
Let me out of here.

20:04.454 --> 20:07.499
Give me some semblance of freedom.
Let me sleep in a bed,

20:07.582 --> 20:09.793
eat with utensils,
and I give you my word

20:09.876 --> 20:13.046
I'll tell you everything...
— see, there's the problem.

20:13.130 --> 20:14.923
I don't trust your word.

20:16.633 --> 20:17.926
All right, then.

20:23.598 --> 20:26.852
I guess I'll have to show you.

20:43.702 --> 20:45.912
I hope this is good.

20:45.996 --> 20:49.124
I don't know much about wine.
I swiped this off the sub.

21:07.726 --> 21:09.895
I wish we could do this all the time.

21:11.521 --> 21:15.317
I hate that we have to be so... private.

21:16.067 --> 21:18.820
What's the matter with being private?

21:18.904 --> 21:23.158
It's ridiculous. I've been sleeping
on the couch for a year.

21:23.241 --> 21:25.410
Why am I not just telling her?

21:26.912 --> 21:29.206
I don't think it's a good idea.

21:36.588 --> 21:37.631
Why not?

21:40.091 --> 21:41.676
Ben wouldn't like it.

21:41.760 --> 21:44.721
That's what this is about?
You're worried about Ben?

21:46.681 --> 21:48.767
Why, because he has a crush on you?

21:50.769 --> 21:53.063
You know?
— come on, everyone knows.

21:53.146 --> 21:55.273
He follows you around like a puppy.

21:56.650 --> 21:59.069
And you don't think that's a problem?

21:59.611 --> 22:03.865
A little less than a kilometer from here
he has me working with chemicals

22:03.949 --> 22:08.161
that could kill every man, woman
and child if I flipped the wrong switch.

22:09.454 --> 22:11.665
Trust me, Ben has enough on his plate.

22:11.748 --> 22:14.084
The last thing he cares about
is you and me.

22:14.876 --> 22:16.670
I just...

22:16.753 --> 22:19.172
Get the feeling
that he would be upset.

22:21.424 --> 22:23.301
What's Ben gonna do?

22:34.980 --> 22:36.898
Goodwin!

22:38.692 --> 22:41.695
You see where the tail landed?
— probably in the water.

22:41.778 --> 22:45.448
You can make that shore in an hour.
Ethan, get up to that fuselage.

22:45.532 --> 22:47.576
There may actually be survivors.

22:47.659 --> 22:50.745
And you're one of 'em.
A passenger. You're in shock.

22:50.829 --> 22:53.957
Come up with a story if they ask.
Stay quiet if they don't.

22:54.040 --> 22:58.670
Listen. Learn. Don't get involved.
I want lists in three days. Go.

23:17.939 --> 23:21.401
Something's wrong. We should've
caught up with them by now.

23:21.484 --> 23:24.029
These people base—jumped
out of a helicopter.

23:24.112 --> 23:26.323
Let's give them
the benefit of the doubt.

23:26.406 --> 23:28.199
[Groaning]

23:31.369 --> 23:33.747
Hey. Hey.

23:33.830 --> 23:35.874
It's ok. Hey. It's all right.

23:35.957 --> 23:37.167
It's ok.

23:37.250 --> 23:38.793
Hey.

23:40.503 --> 23:43.173
It's ok. You're all right. Come on.

23:44.132 --> 23:45.967
Take it easy.

23:46.051 --> 23:47.427
Take it easy.

23:50.472 --> 23:53.683
I'll go get her some water.
— yeah. Thanks.

23:58.647 --> 24:00.065
What happened?

24:02.192 --> 24:04.653
I was going back to the beach and...

24:05.403 --> 24:09.366
I ran into Faraday
and that woman, um, Charlotte.

24:10.992 --> 24:14.287
They disappeared out of camp
last night. Trying to catch up.

24:17.082 --> 24:19.334
Do you know where they were headed?

24:19.417 --> 24:23.129
Some sort of... power station.

24:26.466 --> 24:28.426
They had gas masks.

24:33.223 --> 24:34.557
Juliet.

24:36.476 --> 24:38.019
Juliet!

24:45.568 --> 24:47.070
Juliet!

24:50.407 --> 24:51.825
Juliet!

25:00.333 --> 25:02.460
All right, no tricks.

25:03.795 --> 25:07.340
You're not leading me out
into the jungle so you can disappear

25:07.424 --> 25:10.051
or shoot me in the back.

25:10.135 --> 25:11.511
No tricks, John.

25:11.594 --> 25:14.139
We don't even have to leave
the living room.

25:15.974 --> 25:17.559
So let's have it.

25:19.018 --> 25:20.437
We have a deal, right?

25:21.646 --> 25:25.608
How do I know you won't run off and
meet your people first chance you get?

25:25.692 --> 25:30.405
If my people still wanted me they'd
have stormed this camp long ago.

25:34.451 --> 25:36.661
It's behind that picture.

25:50.091 --> 25:52.177
Thirty-six, 15, 28.

26:17.327 --> 26:18.828
“Red sox“?

26:19.287 --> 26:21.414
I taped over the game.

26:29.798 --> 26:31.549
[Machine whirring]

26:49.400 --> 26:51.027
This is Charles Widmore.

26:53.696 --> 26:56.741
This is the man whose boat
is parked offshore.

26:59.994 --> 27:03.581
This is the man that's been trying
to find the island.

27:12.215 --> 27:15.468
One of my people that had
the misfortune to get caught.

27:15.552 --> 27:19.013
How does Widmore know of the island?
— I don't know, but he does.

27:21.766 --> 27:24.435
John, three months ago
in gainesville, Florida,

27:24.519 --> 27:27.313
the virgin Mary seemed to appear
in a patch of mold

27:27.397 --> 27:29.858
on the side of an old housing complex.

27:29.941 --> 27:34.654
When word got out, over 5,000 people
came to see her face for themselves.

27:34.737 --> 27:37.949
You've survived an airline crash
on this island.

27:38.032 --> 27:42.203
One minute you're in a wheelchair,
the next doing jumping Jacks.

27:42.287 --> 27:44.706
If 5,000 people came out
to see a piece of mold,

27:44.789 --> 27:48.293
how many people do you think
would come out to see you?

27:52.171 --> 27:54.591
Charles Widmore
wants to exploit this island.

27:54.674 --> 27:57.176
He'll do everything in his power
to possess it.

28:14.611 --> 28:18.406
Everything I know about Charles Widmore
is contained in this file.

28:18.489 --> 28:22.410
Some of it's vague, some of it's
guesswork, some of it's concrete,

28:22.493 --> 28:25.330
but this is everything,
and now it's all yours.

28:29.959 --> 28:32.545
I'm sorry I didn't tell
you all this sooner...

28:34.964 --> 28:37.717
But it was the only
bargaining chip I had left.

28:40.428 --> 28:42.513
There's one more thing I need to know.

28:44.599 --> 28:48.895
Your man on the boat,
I want you to tell me who it is.

28:51.898 --> 28:53.608
All right.

28:54.859 --> 28:56.945
But you might want to sit down.

29:05.119 --> 29:07.080
She came through here.

29:07.872 --> 29:10.333
So did they, about
half an hour ahead of her.

29:12.961 --> 29:15.088
What happened? — sorry?

29:15.171 --> 29:17.090
At Locke's. Why did you stay?

29:19.008 --> 29:22.053
I stayed because I had
to find something out.

29:22.136 --> 29:23.471
Are you gonna tell me

29:23.554 --> 29:27.475
or are we gonna keep walking through
the jungle like it doesn't matter?

29:34.899 --> 29:38.444
I stayed to find out if the people
on the freighter know who I am.

29:38.528 --> 29:41.114
If they knew that I'm a fugitive...

29:41.197 --> 29:43.199
That I'm wanted for murder.

29:44.742 --> 29:46.703
Do they?

29:47.662 --> 29:49.580
Yeah, they know.

29:52.125 --> 29:53.835
We should keep moving.

29:53.918 --> 29:55.920
God knows where Juliet is.

30:17.608 --> 30:19.193
[Squeaking]

30:22.572 --> 30:23.990
[Door banging]

30:34.083 --> 30:36.002
Hi, come on in.

30:37.211 --> 30:40.673
Sorry, have to get this ham
out of the oven, or it'll dry out.

30:40.757 --> 30:42.592
Please, don't mind me.

30:42.675 --> 30:45.636
How are you feeling, by the way?
— never better.

30:48.431 --> 30:49.974
Smells delicious.

30:53.895 --> 30:56.022
Ben, I thought this was a dinner party.

30:56.105 --> 30:57.356
Just you and me.

30:59.609 --> 31:01.903
I guess I should've made that clearer.

31:04.155 --> 31:07.325
No, it's fine.
I hope you like dinner rolls.

31:09.494 --> 31:12.080
[Opera playing]

31:14.332 --> 31:18.086
I want to thank you for how wonderful
you've been with Zach and Emma.

31:18.169 --> 31:20.505
They're really sweet kids.

31:22.924 --> 31:28.012
Ben, they've been asking me
about their mother in Los Angeles.

31:28.096 --> 31:31.516
I'm not really sure what to say.
— they'll stop asking in time.

31:32.350 --> 31:34.310
They're children.

31:34.393 --> 31:36.020
Do they really belong here?

31:36.896 --> 31:38.606
They're on the list, Juliet.

31:38.689 --> 31:42.026
Who are we to question
who's on the list and who's not?

31:44.028 --> 31:48.282
Now that we have everyone on the list
for the tail section what about goodwin?

31:50.660 --> 31:52.954
He's been undercover for three weeks.

31:57.166 --> 31:59.710
He's making a case
for this woman, Ana Lucia.

32:01.212 --> 32:04.173
He thinks she'd be
a valuable member of our society.

32:04.257 --> 32:06.551
But between you and me,
I don't see it.

32:06.634 --> 32:09.804
He feels very passionately about her.

32:10.388 --> 32:12.557
Almost inappropriately so.

32:13.599 --> 32:15.476
After losing Ethan, it's a risk.

32:15.560 --> 32:18.437
Goodwin stays where he's at
right now, Juliet.

32:18.521 --> 32:22.650
There's no reason for him
to hurry back, right?

32:22.733 --> 32:26.404
But his assignment will be over soon.
I promise you.

32:29.115 --> 32:31.325
[Alarm sounding]

32:31.409 --> 32:35.329
[Female voice] Warning:
Computer switching to manual operation.

32:35.413 --> 32:37.582
This attempt is unauthorized.

32:50.845 --> 32:54.932
Warning: Manual entry.
Override denied.

32:56.100 --> 33:00.354
Warning: Manual entry.
Override denied.

33:00.438 --> 33:03.691
Repeated attempts to access
storage tanks

33:03.774 --> 33:05.943
will result in contamination.

33:09.614 --> 33:12.033
Repeated attempts to access
storage tanks...

33:12.116 --> 33:13.242
_ hey! [Gasps]

33:17.246 --> 33:20.958
Juliet, what are you doing here?

33:25.463 --> 33:26.505
[Alarm sounding]

33:26.589 --> 33:27.965
Final warning.

33:28.049 --> 33:30.509
Manual override failed.

33:30.593 --> 33:35.014
Step away from the computer.
— I'm so sorry. I can't do that.

33:35.097 --> 33:38.935
Manual override failed.
Counter—measures will begin.

33:42.605 --> 33:44.941
One minute to contamination.

33:46.317 --> 33:49.028
Wanna release the gas?
You'll die with the rest of us.

33:49.111 --> 33:53.366
No, no. I'm not trying to release it.
I'm trying to render it inert.

33:53.449 --> 33:56.953
Juliet, I just want to make it safe.

33:59.247 --> 34:00.414
[Grunting]

34:00.498 --> 34:02.750
Forty seconds to contamination.

34:13.970 --> 34:16.597
Thirty seconds to contamination.

34:22.478 --> 34:25.231
Warning: Contamination imminent.

34:25.314 --> 34:26.941
Evacuate immediately.

34:27.024 --> 34:30.778
[Grunting] — [Faraday] Hey!

34:41.497 --> 34:43.666
Twenty seconds to contamination.

34:43.749 --> 34:46.252
Whatever he's doing, tell him to stop.

34:46.335 --> 34:49.672
We're trying to disable it
before he can use it against us.

34:50.464 --> 34:52.049
Juliet...

34:53.092 --> 34:55.720
Look me in the eye
and tell me you are certain

34:55.803 --> 34:59.640
Benjamin Linus wouldn't use this gas
to kill everyone on this island!

34:59.724 --> 35:01.976
We know he's used it before.

35:02.059 --> 35:04.478
If you wanna stop us,
you have to shoot us both.

35:04.562 --> 35:06.230
Ten seconds to contamination.

35:06.314 --> 35:08.149
Daniel! — yeah, I'm trying.

35:09.900 --> 35:12.069
Come on!

35:12.153 --> 35:13.154
Come on!

35:13.237 --> 35:14.280
Five...

35:15.197 --> 35:16.574
Four...

35:17.408 --> 35:19.410
Three...

35:19.493 --> 35:21.329
Two...

35:23.414 --> 35:26.417
[Computer tone]

35:29.754 --> 35:32.256
[Pressure valves hissing]

35:50.649 --> 35:54.111
That... that was a close one.

36:02.828 --> 36:04.288
[Knocking on door]

36:15.674 --> 36:18.010
What are you reading?
— Shephard's file.

36:18.094 --> 36:19.637
Mikhail dropped it off.

36:22.264 --> 36:24.433
He's a spinal surgeon, Ben.

36:24.517 --> 36:27.478
He has extensive experience
in tumor removal.

36:30.981 --> 36:33.067
How about that?
— he can help you.

36:39.990 --> 36:43.744
I thought you'd be more excited.
What's wrong?

36:47.581 --> 36:49.583
I need you to come with me.

36:55.840 --> 37:00.511
After our last raid on the tail—section
survivors, they ran off, left the beach.

37:02.096 --> 37:06.350
I sent pickett and Tom to track
their location. They came across this.

37:07.309 --> 37:09.103
I'm sorry, Juliet.

37:09.186 --> 37:11.188
Sorry about what?

37:14.024 --> 37:15.943
Oh, my god.

37:16.569 --> 37:18.362
Oh, my god.

37:18.446 --> 37:21.157
Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

37:22.825 --> 37:24.034
Oh, my god!

37:27.121 --> 37:29.248
Goodwin.

37:29.331 --> 37:31.333
[Sobbing]

37:31.417 --> 37:32.751
What happened?

37:33.878 --> 37:36.797
We don't know.
There weren't any witnesses.

37:36.881 --> 37:40.092
I can only assume they found out
he wasn't one of them.

37:42.011 --> 37:45.890
Guess I should've listened to you.
— why are you showing me this?

37:49.894 --> 37:52.313
Why did you bring me out here?

37:52.855 --> 37:55.399
What, you mean instead of his wife?

38:01.614 --> 38:03.824
You knew this would happen.

38:06.994 --> 38:10.456
You sent him out here because
you knew this would happen.

38:11.123 --> 38:14.919
You wanted this.
You wanted him to die!

38:17.004 --> 38:18.130
Why?

38:19.131 --> 38:21.217
Why?

38:22.801 --> 38:25.012
You're asking me why?

38:25.804 --> 38:30.267
After everything I did to get you here,
everything I've done to keep you here,

38:30.351 --> 38:32.811
how can you possibly not understand...

38:34.813 --> 38:36.815
That you're mine?

38:44.782 --> 38:46.492
Take as much time as you need.

38:53.541 --> 38:55.543
[Sobbing]

39:00.673 --> 39:02.800
[Electrical zapping]

39:11.392 --> 39:14.144
Whoa! Kate, it's all right.
They're on our side.

39:14.228 --> 39:17.898
"Our side," Juliet?
She just knocked me unconscious.

39:17.982 --> 39:21.527
Yeah. I'm very sorry about that,
but I had no choice!

39:24.196 --> 39:27.157
Look, Daniel's inside
securing the facility.

39:27.241 --> 39:30.160
If you come with me,
I'll be more than happy to explain

39:30.244 --> 39:32.496
exactly how we just saved your life!

39:36.458 --> 39:38.419
All right, let's go.

39:42.214 --> 39:44.216
I'll take their word for it.

39:53.017 --> 39:54.685
You ok?

39:59.315 --> 40:01.275
He wanted me to kill them.

40:04.361 --> 40:06.655
Ben. He told me to kill both of them.

40:12.202 --> 40:15.456
How can he tell you anything?
— I don't know.

40:15.539 --> 40:19.835
But he knew how to get to me, knew where
they were going, what they were doing.

40:19.918 --> 40:21.754
Don't you understand?

40:21.837 --> 40:25.132
These people came here
to wage war against Ben.

40:26.216 --> 40:28.135
And Ben's gonna win, Jack.

40:29.637 --> 40:32.723
And when he does, you don't
want to be anwvhere near me.

40:34.391 --> 40:35.726
Why not?

40:39.271 --> 40:41.398
Because he thinks that I'm his.

40:44.234 --> 40:46.779
And he knows how I feel about you.

41:10.135 --> 41:12.346
He knows where to find me.

41:31.949 --> 41:33.367
Oh!

41:44.628 --> 41:47.339
[Laughing] — son of a bitch!

41:49.174 --> 41:51.468
How'd you get so damn good
at horseshoes?

41:51.593 --> 41:53.804
I don't know. Guess I'm just lucky.

42:01.645 --> 42:03.856
What the hell are you doing out?

42:04.815 --> 42:06.150
See you guys at dinner.
